        "knowledge_point": "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial",
        "problem": "Solve the inequality $-{9}^{2x-4}{x}^{2}<-5\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}-7\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{9}^{2x-4}{x}^{2} & <-5\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}-7\\cdot {9}^{2x-4} \\\\ -{9}^{2x-4}{x}^{2}+5\\cdot {9}^{2x-4}+7\\cdot {9}^{2x-4} & <0 \\\\ (-{x}^{2}+5+7){9}^{2x-4} & <0 \\\\ (12-{x}^{2}){9}^{2x-4} & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by ${9}^{2x-4}$ and solve the resulting inequality using familiar techniques:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-{x}^{2} & <0 \\\\ -{x}^{2} & <-12 \\\\ {x}^{2} & >12 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & >\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |x| & >2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to the inequality above is $x<-2\\sqrt{3}$ or $x>2\\sqrt{3}.$",
