        "knowledge_point_id": "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying Regions Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table",
        "problem": "Consider the function $f(x,y)=-x(y-1)^{2}.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/ef935d673ddc4fa3b66305717f495914c194be2abff63611f8f6be6763e469ce.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/6f2f29dbb53e8c20d963cc48c89af73b1c806985bc77842cbe28b882305ede32.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-x$ | $(y-1)^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,2)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,2)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,0)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/71aceb11f3056308300e3e5c9587d76a281379964caab83f640a6924ffd94298.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |",
